WEBVTT

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:04.310
We made it to Whitesails!

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:06.150
Haven't been here in a while.

00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:07.490
Will?

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:11.140
It's amazing...

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:24.160
The Faraway Paladin

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:47.600
There's no entry inspection or toll?

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:48.920
That's right.

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:52.410
It's the policy of His Excellency 
Ethel, the city's ruler.

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:55.950
Goods enter this city by boat 
in tremendous amounts,

00:01:53.050 --> 00:02:00.300
Episode 9
Whitesails

00:01:55.950 --> 00:02:00.300
and then they're distributed throughout 
Southmark by land and water.

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:04.280
Wouldn't that mean a massive amount 
of goods pass through here?

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:06.840
Yes, and if all of them 
are checked at the gate,

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:09.810
it would be a hotbed for smuggling 
of both goods and people.

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:11.060
I see...

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:13.600
So Ethel imposed docking fees 
for ships and rental fees

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:17.360
for companies setting up shop here 
to make money for the city,

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:21.700
keeping the movement of people and 
goods as unrestricted as possible.

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:22.870
Oh...

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:26.940
<i>It seems like the economy 
is their top priority.</i>

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:29.780
<i>It's a very advanced city, 
with a real sense of freedom.</i>

00:02:30.370 --> 00:02:33.100
Quit talking about all that boring stuff!

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:35.520
It's Will's first time here! 
Let's have fun!

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:37.010
C'mon, this way!

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:42.900
Will, this is the city's biggest market.

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:44.880
Wow... People...

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:46.270
Why is that surprising?

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:47.890
Oh, over there!

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:51.310
Look! These accessories 
are in style right now!

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:52.380
In style?

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:53.820
Yeah!

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:55.890
<i>There are things "in style" here?!</i>

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.890
Is this stone worth a lot?

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:58.110
Aw, jeez, Menel...

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:59.930
<i>That means these people can 
afford to think about fashion!</i>

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:04.450
It's just one shock after another.

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:06.700
Is that...

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:08.170
A street light.

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:09.060
Street light?!

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:10.550
You don't know what those are?

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:12.780
Gosh, Will, you're so behind the times!

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:15.320
Apprentices from the Academy of Sages

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:17.840
come by in the evenings, lighting up posts

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:21.090
that have Words of Light engraved on them.

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:23.730
So the people here have 
light even at night!

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:26.230
It serves as training for 
apprentice sorcerers,

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:29.390
and they earn a little pocket money, too.

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:34.140
That over there is also a large source 
of income for apprentice sorcerers.

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:35.240
What's that?

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:38.960
Even you must know what that is!

00:03:39.350 --> 00:03:42.120
It's the public bathhouse, Balnea!

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:43.470
Balnea?

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:46.080
What's wrong?

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:49.030
<i>A public bathhouse?! They have baths?!</i>

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:53.710
The water's so clean, 
you can see through it.

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:57.130
Yes, that's an effect of the 
Words of Purification.

00:03:57.130 --> 00:04:01.510
Heat

00:03:57.470 --> 00:04:00.420
Instead of the massive amounts of fuel 
it would take to heat the baths,

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:02.670
they use Words of Heat.

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:04.000
I see.

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:08.430
<i>So it's less like a bath and more 
like a sauna and a cold water pool,</i>

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:09.890
<i>but it's still amazing!</i>

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:15.950
The breeze feels so nice.

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:20.550
<i>I used Words of Purification to 
keep up good hygiene on the road,</i>

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:23.180
<i>but it's great to have actual baths.</i>

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:26.710
Boy, it feels good to have 
a bath after so long.

00:04:26.710 --> 00:04:27.870
That's for sure.

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:30.680
I just hope things don't get all messy now.

00:04:31.130 --> 00:04:32.660
What are we doing next?

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:35.340
Next is...

00:04:36.690 --> 00:04:40.330
Man, I'm always so hungry after a bath!

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:44.510
You two must've been starving, huh?

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:46.290
The food is quite good.

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:47.440
Yeah.

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:50.640
I think it could've been a 
little juicier, though.

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:53.160
<i>It's absorbed the flavor 
of the fish so well,</i>

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:54.650
<i>and the saltiness is just right.</i>

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:57.770
<i>I haven't eaten anything like 
this since I left the temple!</i>

00:04:57.770 --> 00:05:00.670
<i>It tastes like... civilization!</i>

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:04.290
It's all so good,

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:07.090
we lost track of the conversation.

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:11.610
This is good, too!

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:13.470
Can I get a refill on this?

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:14.700
Me, too!

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:16.160
Coming right up.

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:19.180
When we're finished eating, 
we'll head to the temple.

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:22.680
Since you're a priest, Will, 
you need to pay your respects, right?

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:24.870
Oh... Yes, you're right.

00:05:27.570 --> 00:05:28.540
Wow...

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:30.630
They spent a lot of money on this.

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:32.710
Jeez, Menel...

00:05:32.710 --> 00:05:34.770
I'll be back as soon as I'm done.

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:36.380
Please wait here for just a bit.

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:42.100
<i>Are temples in cities always this big?</i>

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:45.070
<i>They all look like works of art.</i>

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:47.350
<i>It feels more like a tourist destination.</i>

00:05:48.130 --> 00:05:49.810
Um, excuse me.

00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:51.640
Yes, how can I help you?

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:54.580
Is there a high-ranking priest here?

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:57.460
I've received divine protection 
and become a priest,

00:05:57.460 --> 00:05:59.020
so I wanted to pay my respects.

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:03.010
Ah... Pardon my asking, 
but which deity do you serve?

00:06:03.010 --> 00:06:05.600
Gracefeel, the goddess of light.

00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:09.810
Oh... The goddess of light? 
That is a problem...

00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:11.010
Why?

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:13.230
Priests of the goddess of 
light are quite uncommon,

00:06:13.230 --> 00:06:16.730
so our rules compel me to use 
the Prayer of Faith Detection.

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:18.470
Okay, that's fine.

00:06:18.820 --> 00:06:20.580
<i>I guess that makes sense.</i>

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:23.080
<i>It's inevitable that people 
would be skeptical</i>

00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:24.760
<i>of a priest to a minor god.</i>

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:27.530
<i>I could be a priest to an 
evil god in disguise.</i>

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:31.310
The thing is... all those 
with the divine protection

00:06:31.310 --> 00:06:34.940
that qualifies them to determine 
another's faith are out right now.

00:06:34.940 --> 00:06:36.470
They're all out?

00:06:36.470 --> 00:06:41.370
Yes. Attacks by demon beasts have been 
on the rise everywhere recently.

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:44.960
All but the vice bishop are 
extremely busy at the moment.

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:46.030
<i>Vice...?</i>

00:06:46.030 --> 00:06:48.750
What are you doing in the 
middle of the aisle?

00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:50.290
Bishop Bagley!

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:52.760
I asked you what you're doing!

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:54.790
Uh, well... j-just...

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:56.570
It's an honor to meet you.

00:06:56.570 --> 00:06:59.180
I am William G. Maryblood.

00:06:59.530 --> 00:07:03.040
I have earned the divine protection 
of Gracefeel, goddess of light,

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:06.430
and have come to the temple of 
Whitesails to pay my respects.

00:07:07.770 --> 00:07:08.730
Hmm...

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:12.700
Bart Bagley. I am in charge of this temple.

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:14.480
Gracefeel...

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:17.930
The goddess of light, a deity 
who has been all but lost?

00:07:17.930 --> 00:07:21.400
And how do I know that you are not some 
suspicious individual using her name

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:23.570
for some insidious plot?

00:07:23.570 --> 00:07:25.880
You have every right to be suspicious.

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:28.500
Is there anything I can 
bless to prove myself?

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:32.770
Hah! You novices are so quick to 
rely on your divine protection!

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:38.110
Listen to me. Divine protection is 
not something to be used lightly,

00:07:38.110 --> 00:07:40.470
nor is it something to use ostentatiously.

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:43.110
<i>He has a point.</i>

00:07:43.110 --> 00:07:46.040
<i>Gus said the same thing about using magic.</i>

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:49.500
<i>I was using my blessing without concern 
since it poses little risk, but...</i>

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:52.310
You are right, of course.

00:07:52.310 --> 00:07:55.340
I truly thank you for reminding 
me of my lack of exper—

00:07:55.340 --> 00:07:56.070
Hmph!

00:07:56.070 --> 00:07:59.440
What are the teachings of the 
goddess of light to you?

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:01.670
Light can only exist where 
there is darkness,

00:08:01.670 --> 00:08:03.730
words can only exist 
where there is silence,

00:08:03.730 --> 00:08:06.460
and life can only exist 
where there is death.

00:08:08.470 --> 00:08:12.330
You. Put his name in the registry 
and show him around the temple.

00:08:12.330 --> 00:08:13.100
What?

00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:17.100
But we haven't performed the Prayer of Faith 
Detection or the Prayer of Lie Detection...

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:17.750
Fool!

00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:20.220
What did I just say, you imbecile?!

00:08:20.510 --> 00:08:24.850
I need to make an appearance at 
the Weaver's Guild banquet.

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:28.270
Spend your time as you please, 
but do not cause any trouble.

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:30.610
And do offer some money.

00:08:31.950 --> 00:08:34.360
W-Well, then, right this way.

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:35.440
R-Right.

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:40.910
How unpleasant it must have been for 
you to have met Bishop Bagley.

00:08:40.910 --> 00:08:42.900
But you handled yourself very well.

00:08:42.900 --> 00:08:43.700
Huh?

00:08:43.700 --> 00:08:47.840
Well, the head of the temple loses himself 
in parties and pleasure-seeking.

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:49.670
He's quick to anger and 
complains constantly.

00:08:49.670 --> 00:08:52.530
Despite all he says, 
he never uses his blessing.

00:08:52.850 --> 00:08:56.340
The vice bishop, on the other hand, 
is a wonderful, virtuous person.

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:56.920
Um...

00:08:58.020 --> 00:09:00.680
Oh, dear, I'm sorry! 
Don't tell anyone I said that!

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:01.660
Sure...

00:09:02.760 --> 00:09:05.680
Hey, what do you know about 
the head of the temple?

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:09.180
Hmm... I haven't heard many 
good things about him.

00:09:09.180 --> 00:09:10.720
Like, they say he's vulgar.

00:09:10.720 --> 00:09:12.900
He seems to have some 
sort of influence behind-the-scenes

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:16.080
of the city's commercial and 
industrial guilds, as well.

00:09:16.310 --> 00:09:18.520
So that's how he's seen around here?

00:09:18.520 --> 00:09:20.560
Still, talk about living it up!

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:23.090
I can't believe he let us use 
the temple's guest room!

00:09:23.090 --> 00:09:24.700
Two of them, even!

00:09:24.700 --> 00:09:27.080
Anyway, what shall we do next?

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:30.250
We could take in the sights, 
or visit some guilds...

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:33.190
Oh, if we do that, I'd recommend the...

00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:35.420
Hang on. Something's going on outside.

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:37.850
That's not the bell that gives the time. 
They're hammering it...

00:09:37.850 --> 00:09:39.160
Is there a fire or something?

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:41.420
It's an emergency alert.

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:44.110
It's a wyvern! Everybody run!

00:09:44.110 --> 00:09:45.000
What?

00:10:01.430 --> 00:10:03.570
Move! Be ready for anything!

00:10:03.570 --> 00:10:06.280
Someone come help us! 
A person's pinned under rubble!

00:10:06.280 --> 00:10:07.920
Ow, ow, ow!

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:09.350
What's going on?!

00:10:08.300 --> 00:10:10.080
Don't push! Please stop pushing!

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:11.950
Has anyone seen my child?!

00:10:11.950 --> 00:10:13.250
Oh, gods...

00:10:21.560 --> 00:10:23.720
Will, wait! Will!

00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:31.930
<i>Why is a wyvern here?</i>

00:10:33.930 --> 00:10:34.950
Fire!

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:40.540
<i>He said all the high-ranking 
clergy are out right now...</i>

00:10:46.150 --> 00:10:48.530
<i>Their civilization... Their city...</i>

00:10:48.950 --> 00:10:51.230
<i>Everything the three of them protected...</i>

00:10:51.230 --> 00:10:53.540
<i>The place where people can live freely...</i>

00:10:56.560 --> 00:10:57.380
Verba!

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:57.170
Words

00:10:57.380 --> 00:10:58.210
Volanto!

00:10:57.420 --> 00:10:57.920
Fly

00:10:58.170 --> 00:10:58.920
Thunder

00:10:58.210 --> 00:10:59.400
Tonitrus!

00:11:01.100 --> 00:11:02.280
<i>It missed!</i>

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:06.590
<i>But those are the longest-ranged 
Words I can use!</i>

00:11:06.840 --> 00:11:09.590
<i>Then I'll just have to keep 
firing until I hit it!</i>

00:11:09.590 --> 00:11:11.660
You idiot! What are you doing?!

00:11:11.660 --> 00:11:14.920
Why are you shooting off high magic 
like that in a blind fury?!

00:11:14.920 --> 00:11:16.070
You'll get yourself killed!

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:16.720
But—

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:17.560
No buts!

00:11:17.560 --> 00:11:21.110
You're fighting a wyvern! 
I'm telling you to be more efficient!

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:23.690
You've got smarts, so use 'em, moron!

00:11:23.690 --> 00:11:25.340
Don't just rush in!

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:31.030
You'll start by learning how to use 
minor magic skillfully and accurately.

00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:33.770
Right.

00:11:33.770 --> 00:11:34.790
Good.

00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:39.700
<i>Think. What can I do about this 
wyvern using what I know?</i>

00:11:41.310 --> 00:11:43.440
Menel, would you help me?

00:11:43.440 --> 00:11:45.460
I need you and your fairies.

00:11:45.460 --> 00:11:46.190
Sure.

00:11:46.900 --> 00:11:48.400
Bee, Tonio!

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:52.610
Work with the people nearby to get everyone 
clear of the temple's front garden!

00:11:52.610 --> 00:11:54.760
I'm going to bring the wyvern down there!

00:11:54.760 --> 00:11:55.690
Your Excellency!

00:11:55.690 --> 00:11:57.910
You must take shelter below, quickly!

00:11:57.910 --> 00:11:59.440
How could this happen?

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:02.790
Dozens of people... hundreds of 
people... are going to die.

00:12:04.360 --> 00:12:05.940
Now, then...

00:12:05.940 --> 00:12:09.000
Sylphs, Sylphs, maidens of wind.

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:11.170
Your steps are the wind's steps.

00:12:11.170 --> 00:12:13.020
Your song is the wind's song.

00:12:13.450 --> 00:12:16.930
Sing in chorus, sing in rounds, 
cheer and applaud.

00:12:17.320 --> 00:12:21.640
Your harmony shall spread the Words 
of Origin in the ten directions.

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:22.420
Words

00:12:21.890 --> 00:12:22.780
Verba.

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:23.380
Fly

00:12:22.780 --> 00:12:23.770
Volanto.

00:12:23.770 --> 00:12:24.830
Conciliat.

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:24.640
Unite

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:25.510
Follow

00:12:24.830 --> 00:12:25.630
Sequitur.

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:26.640
Thunder

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:26.870
Tonitrus...

00:12:26.870 --> 00:12:27.770
Araneum!

00:12:26.890 --> 00:12:27.640
Spiderweb

00:12:37.820 --> 00:12:40.140
Is that... magic?

00:12:40.140 --> 00:12:43.260
There's a fairy user, too? 
Boy, are we lucky!

00:12:43.260 --> 00:12:45.520
We've got this! We can do it! Hurry!

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:52.380
<i>I'm probably not hurting it that much.</i>

00:12:54.600 --> 00:12:55.650
<i>But that's fine.</i>

00:12:56.060 --> 00:12:58.620
<i>So long as the wyvern identifies 
us as its enemies.</i>

00:12:58.620 --> 00:13:01.550
<i>Almost all beasts of this 
type are highly aggressive.</i>

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:03.650
<i>Even in situations where 
they could get away,</i>

00:13:03.650 --> 00:13:05.530
<i>they'll choose to take the offensive.</i>

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:06.750
Here it comes.

00:13:06.750 --> 00:13:07.390
Right.

00:13:09.230 --> 00:13:14.470
<i>The rest depends on how close 
my skills have come to theirs.</i>

00:13:14.910 --> 00:13:18.440
<i>Goddess, I now fight for 
the sake of my oath.</i>

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:21.760
<i>To banish evil and save the suffering.</i>

00:13:21.760 --> 00:13:23.850
<i>Pray! Pray!</i>

00:13:23.850 --> 00:13:25.860
<i>Be as unbreakable as adamantine!</i>

00:13:25.860 --> 00:13:28.460
<i>For eternity... For all eternity...</i>

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:31.200
<i>Reject all that is evil!</i>

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:33.780
On the flame of Gracefeel!

00:13:43.660 --> 00:13:45.560
What the heck is that?!

00:13:51.310 --> 00:13:54.820
Sylphs! Beautiful maidens of 
wind, dancers in the gale!

00:13:54.820 --> 00:13:57.810
Show those foolish enough to fancy themselves

00:13:57.810 --> 00:14:00.100
better dancers the bitter taste of earth!

00:14:05.280 --> 00:14:06.310
Ligatur!

00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:06.150
Be Tied

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:07.030
Knot

00:14:06.310 --> 00:14:07.030
Nodus!

00:14:07.030 --> 00:14:08.470
Obligatio!

00:14:07.150 --> 00:14:08.240
Binding

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:12.130
It's bound!

00:14:12.130 --> 00:14:15.300
No, it's trying to tear them off! 
Damn, it's strong!

00:14:15.900 --> 00:14:17.210
Acceleratio!

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:17.080
Accelerate

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:22.000
All right!

00:14:25.290 --> 00:14:26.590
No way...

00:14:26.910 --> 00:14:28.470
<i>That didn't finish it off?!</i>

00:14:29.420 --> 00:14:31.380
Run! It's gonna use its breath!

00:14:31.700 --> 00:14:33.520
<i>There are still people back there.</i>

00:14:33.520 --> 00:14:35.890
<i>What do I do? What can I do?!</i>

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:39.400
Get 'em!

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:41.220
Acceleratio!

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:41.110
Accelerate

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:46.440
<i>If you don't know, use your muscles!</i>

00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:48.990
<i>Be violent! Get 'em!</i>

00:14:56.740 --> 00:14:57.870
A n-neck throw?!

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:03.530
You're not getting away!

00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:11.560
Your fangs and claws will harm no one!

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:32.150
Well done! Excellent work!

00:15:32.150 --> 00:15:38.160
I give thanks to all the gods for allowing 
me to serve a hero such as you!

00:15:38.160 --> 00:15:42.790
It's the birth of a new Wyvern Killer! 
A brand new hero!

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:45.420
Sing his praises with your applause!

00:15:49.620 --> 00:15:50.630
Thank you!

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:51.960
Thank you!

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:53.960
Thank you!

00:15:57.690 --> 00:15:59.630
I guess we were too late, huh?

00:16:00.220 --> 00:16:02.770
Still, I had no idea so many magic users

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:05.980
and a warrior strong enough to 
kill a wyvern were staying here!

00:16:05.980 --> 00:16:08.030
It is truly divine providence!

00:16:15.340 --> 00:16:18.050
I guess anything goes with you, huh?

00:16:18.050 --> 00:16:19.210
You're surprised?

00:16:19.210 --> 00:16:21.180
I'm used to the way you defy logic.

00:16:22.940 --> 00:16:26.310
Well, I was reminded of 
how inexperienced I am.

00:16:26.310 --> 00:16:26.800
Huh?

00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:29.000
It was great for a first attempt,

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:31.180
but I was just lucky to 
land a surprise attack.

00:16:31.180 --> 00:16:34.330
And what was that black miasma around it?

00:16:34.330 --> 00:16:35.000
Hey!

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:36.850
You brought down a real monster!

00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:39.130
Critique yourself all you want, 
but at least be a little bit happy.

00:16:39.130 --> 00:16:41.430
It's hard for me to be happy if you're not.

00:16:41.860 --> 00:16:42.690
Okay.

00:16:43.350 --> 00:16:44.970
<i>When he puts it that way...</i>

00:16:44.970 --> 00:16:46.840
<i>There's a lot I could've done better,</i>

00:16:46.840 --> 00:16:49.520
<i>but now I'm a Wyvern Killer 
like the three of them.</i>

00:16:49.910 --> 00:16:51.970
<i>That makes me happy.</i>

00:16:52.190 --> 00:16:53.880
Yeah... Yeah.

00:16:53.880 --> 00:16:56.940
Thanks, Menel! I owe it all to you!

00:16:56.940 --> 00:16:58.790
Yeah. We did it, man.

00:17:00.280 --> 00:17:04.170
Also, you know damn well it was 
nearly all your doing, idiot!

00:17:05.870 --> 00:17:07.370
Wyvern Killer!

00:17:08.190 --> 00:17:10.480
Yes, that's me! What can I do for you?

00:17:10.480 --> 00:17:12.380
Please come with me, quickly!

00:17:12.380 --> 00:17:13.790
Uh...

00:17:13.790 --> 00:17:17.600
The crown prince wishes to see you.

00:17:18.720 --> 00:17:22.240
Welcome to my mansion, hero.

00:17:22.590 --> 00:17:27.730
<i>So this is the crown prince of the 
Fertile Kingdom, the lord of Whitesails,</i>

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:29.800
<i>and the ruler of Southmark...</i>

00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:35.730
It is a greater honor than I deserve 
to stand in Your Highness's presence.

00:17:35.730 --> 00:17:38.630
I have come here per your request.

00:17:38.630 --> 00:17:41.020
My name is William G. Maryblood.

00:17:41.020 --> 00:17:44.290
Oh? You are well-versed 
in the old etiquette.

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:46.370
I assume you are of high birth?

00:17:46.370 --> 00:17:48.180
No, um...

00:17:48.180 --> 00:17:51.330
If Your Highness could please refrain 
from asking about my origins...

00:17:52.370 --> 00:17:55.470
You have your circumstances, then. 
I understand.

00:17:57.660 --> 00:17:59.400
Please, have a seat.

00:17:59.400 --> 00:18:00.290
Thank you.

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:18.120
William, there are four or five 
in your group, are there not?

00:18:18.120 --> 00:18:19.660
Yes, four of us.

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:23.990
Which makes you a magic user, a priest, 
a fairy user, and a warrior?

00:18:23.990 --> 00:18:24.660
Huh?

00:18:26.240 --> 00:18:31.060
A traveling priest, hunter, 
merchant, and bard, actually.

00:18:32.010 --> 00:18:35.780
One who shot lightning at the wyvern, 
one who made a wall of light,

00:18:35.780 --> 00:18:39.390
one who controlled air currents, 
and one who broke its neck.

00:18:39.390 --> 00:18:40.640
That makes four, no?

00:18:40.640 --> 00:18:44.550
If that makes four people, 
it is indeed correct we are two of them.

00:18:45.250 --> 00:18:46.540
What does that mean?

00:18:46.540 --> 00:18:48.820
My friend there, Meneldor, 
called the fairies,

00:18:48.820 --> 00:18:51.560
spread Words, 
and manipulated the air currents

00:18:51.560 --> 00:18:54.930
to bring the wyvern down to the ground.

00:18:54.930 --> 00:18:58.050
So he is the fairy user, then?

00:18:58.050 --> 00:18:59.030
And the rest?

00:18:59.030 --> 00:19:00.660
Was me.

00:19:03.030 --> 00:19:06.790
I'm sorry, but would you mind 
telling me what you did?

00:19:09.600 --> 00:19:12.870
I used brute force to break its neck.

00:19:12.870 --> 00:19:15.790
You kill a wyvern and feel no pride?

00:19:15.790 --> 00:19:18.380
You really are a warrior 
of unparalleled bravery.

00:19:18.380 --> 00:19:19.450
Uh...

00:19:20.330 --> 00:19:23.420
Does anything need to be done to fix 
the damage that the wyvern caused?

00:19:23.740 --> 00:19:27.050
Of course, work has already been 
done, and more is yet to come.

00:19:27.310 --> 00:19:30.760
But there is something more 
important that must be done.

00:19:30.990 --> 00:19:35.420
Yes. Offering my thanks to 
the hero, for example.

00:19:35.420 --> 00:19:36.780
No, I—

00:19:36.780 --> 00:19:38.520
Do not be modest.

00:19:38.520 --> 00:19:41.820
I do not want my people to see 
me as an ungrateful man.

00:19:42.890 --> 00:19:48.510
I, Ethelbald, thank you both on behalf 
of the people of Whitesails.

00:19:49.150 --> 00:19:53.960
You did well to minimize the damage 
caused by a wyvern's surprise attack.

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:56.620
I am unworthy of such praise.

00:19:57.460 --> 00:20:01.550
I would like to give you a reward. 
Is there anything you want?

00:20:03.900 --> 00:20:08.730
I traveled here today via 
Beast Woods to the south.

00:20:09.090 --> 00:20:11.480
The villages in that area 
are currently under threat

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:15.390
by an army of demons commanding 
savage demon beasts.

00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:19.220
Um, if I may ask...

00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:21.730
Would it be possible for Your Highness

00:20:21.730 --> 00:20:24.890
to send soldiers to hunt down the demons?

00:20:24.890 --> 00:20:26.690
It's not impossible,

00:20:26.690 --> 00:20:28.500
but it would be difficult.

00:20:28.500 --> 00:20:30.500
You saw that wyvern.

00:20:30.500 --> 00:20:32.740
Demon beasts much like it have 
been causing frequent incidents

00:20:32.740 --> 00:20:35.330
within the parts of 
Southmark that I govern.

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:36.700
You mean...

00:20:36.700 --> 00:20:39.290
Yes. It's that toxic miasma.

00:20:39.730 --> 00:20:42.710
Any being it touches is corrupted 
by the poison and turns savage.

00:20:43.230 --> 00:20:45.800
Are you certain you are 
well yourself, William?

00:20:46.130 --> 00:20:48.380
I am naturally resistant to poisons.

00:20:48.380 --> 00:20:50.020
That is good to hear.

00:20:50.500 --> 00:20:52.310
Under the previous king's policies,

00:20:52.310 --> 00:20:54.390
we expanded our domain too much.

00:20:54.390 --> 00:20:59.270
We cannot even sufficiently protect 
the villages we directly govern.

00:20:59.580 --> 00:21:01.680
Do you understand my meaning?

00:21:04.270 --> 00:21:07.150
Then... would you give me permission

00:21:07.150 --> 00:21:09.360
to hire adventurers and 
mercenaries with my own money

00:21:09.360 --> 00:21:12.030
and organize an army to 
drive out the demons?

00:21:14.050 --> 00:21:19.080
William, do you realize 
what that would mean?

00:21:19.080 --> 00:21:23.520
I understand that I am asking 
a great deal of you.

00:21:23.520 --> 00:21:25.670
Yet you stand by your request?

00:21:26.020 --> 00:21:26.770
Yes.

00:21:27.290 --> 00:21:28.820
If I do not,

00:21:28.820 --> 00:21:32.820
how many tragedies would we be 
forced to simply overlook?

00:21:32.820 --> 00:21:37.680
But to save everyone is a task 
not even the gods can achieve.

00:21:42.560 --> 00:21:44.180
Honestly...

00:21:44.180 --> 00:21:48.540
If only you were some nameless man 
making this request of me...

00:21:48.540 --> 00:21:49.940
You are right.

00:21:49.940 --> 00:21:52.580
That said, had I not killed the wyvern,

00:21:52.580 --> 00:21:55.090
I may never have had the opportunity 
to speak with Your Highness.

00:21:55.090 --> 00:21:56.970
That is also true.

00:21:57.300 --> 00:21:58.250
But...

00:21:59.070 --> 00:22:03.030
I must also consider the 
option of killing you.

00:23:35.720 --> 00:23:39.970
Episode 10
Renowned Glory
